1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,041
Welcome to Night 1 of the Cognitive Shutdown Method.

2
00:00:03,991 --> 00:00:10,741
Tonight we begin with the most important rule in all of behavioral sleep medicine: the anchor.

3
00:00:10,741 --> 00:00:13,932
Your wake time matters more than your bedtime.

4
00:00:13,932 --> 00:00:15,344
Here is why.

5
00:00:15,344 --> 00:00:18,991
Your body runs on two systems that govern sleep.

6
00:00:18,991 --> 00:00:23,035
The circadian system tells your brain when it is day or night.

7
00:00:23,035 --> 00:00:30,549
The homeostatic system, also called sleep pressure, accumulates the longer you stay awake.

8
00:00:30,549 --> 00:00:37,873
Both systems depend on one consistent signal to function properly, and that signal is your wake time.

9
00:00:37,873 --> 00:00:44,329
When you sleep in on weekends, even by one hour, you scramble both systems at once.

10
00:00:44,329 --> 00:00:47,138
Cortisol releases at the wrong time.

11
00:00:47,138 --> 00:00:49,108
Melatonin shifts.

12
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:54,329
The brain loses its anchor, and Sunday night insomnia becomes inevitable.

13
00:00:54,329 --> 00:00:56,961
So tonight, you set a wake time.

14
00:00:56,961 --> 00:00:59,182
Not an ambitious one.

15
00:00:59,182 --> 00:01:01,152
A realistic one.

16
00:01:01,152 --> 00:01:04,270
The time you actually need to be up on weekdays.

17
00:01:04,270 --> 00:01:12,152
And starting tomorrow, you keep that wake time every single day, including weekends, for the next seven nights.

18
00:01:12,152 --> 00:01:14,197
This is non-negotiable.

19
00:01:14,197 --> 00:01:16,799
You do not need to change your bedtime yet.

20
00:01:16,799 --> 00:01:18,447
Just the wake time.

21
00:01:18,447 --> 00:01:22,844
The bedtime will adjust naturally as sleep pressure builds.

22
00:01:22,844 --> 00:01:27,226
Now, before you sleep tonight, let us prepare your body.

23
00:01:27,226 --> 00:01:29,535
Find a comfortable position.

24
00:01:29,535 --> 00:01:31,432
Let your shoulders drop.

25
00:01:31,432 --> 00:01:33,241
Let your jaw soften.

26
00:01:33,241 --> 00:01:37,329
Take a slow breath in through your nose for four seconds.

27
00:01:37,329 --> 00:01:38,932
Hold for seven.

28
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:42,814
And release slowly through your mouth for eight seconds.

29
00:01:42,814 --> 00:01:44,123
Once more.

30
00:01:44,123 --> 00:01:45,594
In for four.

31
00:01:45,594 --> 00:01:47,197
Hold for seven.

32
00:01:47,197 --> 00:01:48,564
Out for eight.

33
00:01:48,564 --> 00:01:50,123
One last time.

34
00:01:50,123 --> 00:01:51,594
In for four.

35
00:01:51,594 --> 00:01:53,197
Hold for seven.

36
00:01:53,197 --> 00:01:54,829
Release for eight.

37
00:01:54,829 --> 00:01:57,814
Your wake time tomorrow is now an anchor.

38
00:01:57,814 --> 00:02:00,005
Everything else builds from it.

39
00:02:00,005 --> 00:02:01,344
Sleep well.

